{"id": "mm7225a3", "attempt": "read", "status": "ok", "message_id": "msg_011Cg7nFJnpP7QP81vrCuLL7", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "error_kind": "", "errors": [], "usage": {"input": 37065, "write_1h": 0, "write_5m": 0, "cache_read": 0, "output": 6434}, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"id\":\"mm7225a3\",\"reader\":{\"model\":\"prod\",\"reader_id\":\"prod\",\"role\":\"judgment\"},\"data_focus\":{\"v\":\"yes\",\"ev\":[]},\"outcome_types\":[{\"v\":\"binary/categorical\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Reinfections represented 2.7% of all reported SARS-CoV-2 infections during the Delta variant period in late 2021\"}]},{\"v\":\"continuous\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"The median time to reinfection decreased substantially to 335 days in mid-June 2022 after the start of the BA.4/BA.5 period\"}]}],\"analytic_depth\":[{\"v\":\"summary\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"a total of 2,784,548 laboratory-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 reinfections were reported among adults aged ≥18 years from 18 U.S. jurisdictions, accounting for 12.7%\"}]},{\"v\":\"comparison\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"Increases were more pronounced among adults aged 18–49 years compared with those among older persons.\"}]}],\"procedures\":[],\"comparison\":{\"framework\":\"group\",\"scale\":\"absolute\",\"referent\":null,\"across\":[\"variant period\",\"age group\",\"outcome (cases, hospitalizations, deaths)\"],\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"the percentages of reinfections among all COVID-19 cases, hospitalizations, and deaths reported by 18 U.S. jurisdictions increased substantially as new Omicron lineages became predominant.\"},{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"The absolute increase in the percentage of reinfections among all reported SARS-CoV-2 infections was highest among adults aged 18–49 years\"}]},\"inference\":{\"v\":\"none\",\"method_stated\":false,\"ev\":[]},\"primary_measures\":[{\"v\":\"percentage of reinfections among all infections\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 1\",\"q\":\"Reinfections (% of all infections)\"}]},{\"v\":\"median time to reinfection\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Overall weekly trends in median time to reinfection (i.e., the interval from previous infection to reinfection) were estimated\"}]}],\"regression_fields\":null,\"public_health_question\":{\"v\":\"How did SARS-CoV-2 reinfections, as a percentage of all infections, hospitalizations and deaths, and the interval between infections change across variant periods and age groups among U.S. adults?\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"To describe trends over time, laboratory-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 reinfections and associated severe outcomes were characterized\"}]},\"conditions\":[{\"v\":\"SARS-CoV-2 reinfection\",\"role\":\"outcome\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"title\",\"q\":\"Trends in Laboratory-Confirmed SARS-CoV-2 Reinfections and Associated Hospitalizations and Deaths Among Adults Aged ≥18 Years\"}]},{\"v\":\"COVID-19\",\"role\":\"outcome\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Percentages of reinfections among all COVID-19 cases, hospitalizations, and deaths were calculated by age group and variant period.\"}]}],\"study_design\":[{\"v\":\"surveillance/descriptive\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"This descriptive analysis of surveillance data reported by 18 jurisdictions shows\"}]},{\"v\":\"before/after or trend\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"Cases and severe outcomes associated with SARS-CoV-2 reinfection have increased across the United States since September 2021.\"}]},{\"v\":\"ecologic\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"this ecologic analysis of epidemiologic changes in reinfection by period of SARS-CoV-2 variant predominance could not adjust for important confounders\"}]}],\"data_source_type\":[{\"v\":\"state or local surveillance\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"for all infections and reinfections occurring among adults aged ≥18 years during September 5, 2021–December 31, 2022, were reported by 18 U.S. jurisdictions\"}]}],\"data_source_named\":[{\"v\":\"electronic laboratory reporting\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"including test results from electronic laboratory reporting data, have changed or have been discontinued\"}]}],\"setting\":{\"v\":\"US subnational\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"title\",\"q\":\"18 U.S. Jurisdictions, September 2021–December 2022\"}]},\"vaccine_outcome_type\":null,\"equity\":{\"level\":0,\"level_reason\":\"Age is the only SPD: it bounds the population (≥18 years) and stratifies results, without social-position framing; explanations offered for age differences are exposure, vaccination and survival factors.\",\"level_confidence\":\"high\",\"level_alternative\":{\"level\":2,\"reason\":\"Age-group-specific percentages are reported and described; if age were read as framed socially, group-specific results would reach level 2.\"},\"dimensions\":[{\"v\":\"age\",\"role\":\"population\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"title\",\"q\":\"Among Adults Aged ≥18 Years\"}]},{\"v\":\"age\",\"role\":\"stratifier\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Percentages of reinfections among all COVID-19 cases, hospitalizations, and deaths were calculated by age group and variant period.\"}]}],\"determinants_of_health\":{\"v\":null,\"ev\":[]},\"equity_action\":{\"v\":false,\"ev\":[]},\"equity_measurement\":\"Age collapsed to three groups (18–49, 50–64, ≥65); the Summary contrasts 18–49 with ≥50 years.\"},\"groupwise\":[{\"across\":[\"age\"],\"n_groups\":3,\"ordered\":true,\"assessment\":\"side by side\",\"resolves_to_finer\":false,\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"The absolute increase in the percentage of reinfections among all reported SARS-CoV-2 infections was highest among adults aged 18–49 years\"},{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Among adults aged 50–64 years, the percentage of reinfections among all infections increased from 2.1% (Delta) to 29.0% (Omicron BQ.1/BQ1.1)\"}]}],\"uncertain_fields\":[\"analytic_depth\",\"comparison\"],\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The weekly median time to reinfection weighted by jurisdiction reinfection counts is arithmetic on summary values, not weighting, so no procedures are recorded. Age comparisons within variant periods are read as a series over time by group (comparison), not stratification. Scale is set absolute because claims rank absolute increases, though no difference values are reported.\",\"view_issues\":\"Footnote ¶¶¶ lists Michigan among 13 jurisdictions reporting multiple reinfections, but Michigan is not among the 18 study jurisdictions. Figure 1 caption names panels for cases and hospitalizations only, while its description also mentions deaths.\"}", "type": "text"}]}